{"name":"Dover Plains","hex":"#ccaf92","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Dover Plains","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A hamlet and census-designated place in the town of Dover, Dutchess County, New York, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Dover_Plains"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dover Plains, New York","blocks":[{"text":"Dover Plains is a hamlet and census-designated place (CDP) in Dutchess County, New York, United States. The population was 1,322 at the 2020 census. It is part of the Kiryas Joel–Poughkeepsie–Newburgh, NY Metropolitan Statistical Area."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Downtown_Dover_Plains%2C_NY.jpg/330px-Downtown_Dover_Plains%2C_NY.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dover_Plains%2C_New_York","wikidata":"Q2880028"},{"title":"Dover","blocks":[{"text":"Dover is a town, major ferry port and civil parish in Kent, England. It faces France across the Strait of Dover, the narrowest part of the English Channel at 33 kilometres (21 mi) from Cap Gris-Nez in France. It lies southeast of Canterbury and east of Maidstone. The town is the administrative centre of the Dover District and home of the Port of Dover. In 2024 it had an estimated population of 44,209."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Dover_from_the_top_of_Dover_Castle_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4061940.jpg/330px-Dover_from_the_top_of_Dover_Castle_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4061940.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dover","wikidata":"Q179224"},{"title":"Plain","blocks":[{"text":"In geography, a plain, commonly known as flatland, is a flat expanse of land that generally has few rapid or steep changes in elevation. Natural vegetation in plains can include prairies/grasslands, forests, savanah, tundra, and desert biomes, among others. Plains occur as lowlands along valleys or at the base of mountains, as coastal plains, and as plateaus or uplands. Plains are one of the major landforms on earth, being present on all continents and covering more than one-third of the world's land area. Plains in many areas are important for agriculture. There are various types of plains, and biomes on them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Maniototoevening.jpg/330px-Maniototoevening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plain","wikidata":"Q160091"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Second_Baptist_Church_of_Dover%2C_Dover_Plains%2C_NY.jpg/500px-Second_Baptist_Church_of_Dover%2C_Dover_Plains%2C_NY.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Second_Baptist_Church_of_Dover%2C_Dover_Plains%2C_NY.jpg/1280px-Second_Baptist_Church_of_Dover%2C_Dover_Plains%2C_NY.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Second_Baptist_Church_of_Dover%2C_Dover_Plains%2C_NY.jpg/500px-Second_Baptist_Church_of_Dover%2C_Dover_Plains%2C_NY.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Second Baptist Church of Dover Plains","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASecond_Baptist_Church_of_Dover%2C_Dover_Plains%2C_NY.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/DoverPlainsNY.JPG/500px-DoverPlainsNY.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/DoverPlainsNY.JPG/1280px-DoverPlainsNY.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/DoverPlainsNY.JPG/500px-DoverPla